# Claude Code local, per-machine settings — not meant to be shared/committed
.claude/settings.local.json

# .claude/agents/ and .claude/commands/ ARE tracked -- they're the actual
# functional location Claude Code looks for custom subagents/slash
# commands (a bare agents/ or commands/ folder is documentation only,
# invisible to the harness). Only the per-machine settings file above is
# excluded.

# Your project's own build artefacts go here.
#
# This template is deliberately language-agnostic, so it does NOT guess at a
# stack -- picking __pycache__/ over node_modules/, bin/, obj/ or target/ would
# be arbitrary. But that means a new project's first test run leaves untracked
# junk to clean by hand before its first commit, which two separate testers hit
# independently. Add your stack's entries below on day one and it never comes up
# again.
